  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1110 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nAs we head into the weekend, the upper level low will get swept\naway and our wx will be influenced by a Bermuda high along with a\nseries of weak disturbances. This pattern will bring slightly\nwarmer and more humid conditions along with area-wide chances for\nscattered showers and storms. Dew points will climb into the 70s,\npushing afternoon heat index values over 100, except for the\nPlateau. CAPE values will increase helping to fuel storms, but \nshear and low level forcing will be generally weak. This will keep\nthe severe threat low, but heavy rain will be likely with any \nthunderstorms. \n\nWe won't see any major changes in the weather pattern as we head \ninto early next week. The upper level trough over the Great Lakes \nwill weaken and that will allow a strong upper level ridge over \nthe West to build east some. This will push highs into the low to \nmid 90s with afternoon heat index values above 100. Rain chances \nwill come down some as the upper level ridge to our east flattens \nand pushes south but still could see a few afternoon showers and \nthunderstorms.",
